{
  "comment": "The cases of the interface contract that arm the fault injection points of the core, of http-negotiation and of template, whose error enums the core passes on (binding design G-5, X-1; HY-132.6), in the case form of binding (G-5). The group internal arms front_functions.route_request with the smallest application that routes the request GET / to its page; without the faults the request is the page home. The group template arms rules.template_reads with a template whose else-if branch the parser of template adds to its open block; without the faults the template has its read paths. A case of the group template without faults names a template that is missing and raises invalid_application, the other kind of rules.template_reads (HY-73.2). The group session arms session_store.random for opening_functions.open_page with a file session of the directory of the test that found no record, whose first get makes a new token by the call of random_hex of the core, and raises random; without the faults the page opens with a new token. The case that arms session_store.internal is in core-faults.json, because that point breaks only inside the store, which the package of session-store makes with its own binding_core (binding B2.487). Its other cases give a file session whose file of the case holds a stored value of another form, or a mask that is no token, and raise the kinds of open_page that an input gives (HY-24.14, HY-104.23). A directory is a relative path that the test resolves in a directory of its own, and a file of a case is written there (binding GN-6y, GN-13i).",
